{"id":"238427f0df2ecaed","group":"57","path":"57/57-df-elementary-equivalence.md","title":"Elementary Equivalence","display":"df-elementary-equivalence — Elementary Equivalence","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Mathematical Logic","book_abbrev":"57","label":"57-df-elementary-equivalence","aliases":["57-df-elementary-equivalence"],"display":"df-elementary-equivalence — Elementary Equivalence","depends_on":["[[57-df-structure]]","[[57-df-satisfaction]]","[[57-df-sentence]]","[[57-df-theory]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Mathematical Logic"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"57"},{"key":"label","html":"57-df-elementary-equivalence"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>57-df-elementary-equivalence</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-elementary-equivalence — Elementary Equivalence"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"c136ba3960a7223a\" href=\"?note=c136ba3960a7223a\" title=\"57-df-structure\">57-df-structure</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"03dc48eb29950767\" href=\"?note=03dc48eb29950767\" title=\"57-df-satisfaction\">57-df-satisfaction</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"38cb16fd577caf7b\" href=\"?note=38cb16fd577caf7b\" title=\"57-df-sentence\">57-df-sentence</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"9c053a73bd2d84c4\" href=\"?note=9c053a73bd2d84c4\" title=\"57-df-theory\">57-df-theory</a></span></div>"}],"html":"<h1 id=\"df-elementary-equivalence-—-Elementary-Equivalence-$\\equiv$\">df-elementary-equivalence — Elementary Equivalence <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\equiv\">\\(\\equiv\\)</span></h1>\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A}, \\mathfrak{B}\">\\(\\mathfrak{A}, \\mathfrak{B}\\)</span> (签名 <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"S\">\\(S\\)</span> 上的结构, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"c136ba3960a7223a\" href=\"?note=c136ba3960a7223a\" title=\"57-df-structure\">57-df-structure</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Struct}(\\mathfrak{A}, S), \\mathrm{Struct}(\\mathfrak{B}, S)\">\\(\\mathrm{Struct}(\\mathfrak{A}, S), \\mathrm{Struct}(\\mathfrak{B}, S)\\)</span> (S-结构谓词, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"c136ba3960a7223a\" href=\"?note=c136ba3960a7223a\" title=\"57-df-structure\">57-df-structure</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}elementary\\text{-}equivalence} \\vdash \\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B} \\Leftrightarrow \\forall \\varphi \\in \\mathrm{Sent}_S\\;(\\mathfrak{A} \\models \\varphi \\Leftrightarrow \\mathfrak{B} \\models \\varphi)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}elementary\\text{-}equivalence} \\vdash \\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B} \\Leftrightarrow \\forall \\varphi \\in \\mathrm{Sent}_S\\;(\\mathfrak{A} \\models \\varphi \\Leftrightarrow \\mathfrak{B} \\models \\varphi)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}elementary\\text{-}equivalence} \\vdash \\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B} \\Leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Th}(\\mathfrak{A}) = \\mathrm{Th}(\\mathfrak{B})\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}elementary\\text{-}equivalence} \\vdash \\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B} \\Leftrightarrow \\mathrm{Th}(\\mathfrak{A}) = \\mathrm{Th}(\\mathfrak{B})\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B}\">\\(\\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B}\\)</span> means <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A}\">\\(\\mathfrak{A}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{B}\">\\(\\mathfrak{B}\\)</span> satisfy exactly the same first-order sentences.</li>\n<li>Elementary equivalence is weaker than isomorphism: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A} \\cong \\mathfrak{B} \\Rightarrow \\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B}\">\\(\\mathfrak{A} \\cong \\mathfrak{B} \\Rightarrow \\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B}\\)</span>, but not conversely.</li>\n<li>Relation to <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-7\" data-note=\"f60efdcc5c3b9010\" href=\"?note=f60efdcc5c3b9010\" title=\"57-df-n-equivalence\">57-df-n-equivalence</a>: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B} \\Leftrightarrow \\forall n \\in \\mathbb{N}\\;(\\mathfrak{A} \\equiv_n \\mathfrak{B})\">\\(\\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B} \\Leftrightarrow \\forall n \\in \\mathbb{N}\\;(\\mathfrak{A} \\equiv_n \\mathfrak{B})\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The <strong>Keisler-Shelah Theorem</strong> states: <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B} \\Leftrightarrow\">\\(\\mathfrak{A} \\equiv \\mathfrak{B} \\Leftrightarrow\\)</span> there exists an ultrafilter <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal{U}\">\\(\\mathcal{U}\\)</span> such that <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathfrak{A}^{\\mathcal{U}} \\cong \\mathfrak{B}^{\\mathcal{U}}\">\\(\\mathfrak{A}^{\\mathcal{U}} \\cong \\mathfrak{B}^{\\mathcal{U}}\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>Elementary equivalence is central to model theory and the study of model-theoretic invariants.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"df-elementary-equivalence-—-Elementary-Equivalence-$\\equiv$","text":"df-elementary-equivalence — Elementary Equivalence $\\equiv$","level":1},{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","t